\"benchmarks\", \"workflows\", \"evaluation\", \"multi-step tasks\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"FinPerMA: Personalized-Memory Benchmark for LLM Agents\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Develops a memory benchmark specifically designed for LLM agents to assess personalized information retention and retrieval.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Ben Wang et al.\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"memory\", \"benchmarks\", \"LLM\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"FinProBench: Evaluating Financial AI Agents with Role-Grounded Rubrics\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Creates evaluation metrics for AI agents in professional financial contexts using role-based assessment criteria.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Ben Wang et al.\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"evaluation\", \"financial AI\", \"benchmarks\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"A/B Agent: Self-Evolving Agent for Strategy Iteration\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"Describes an autonomous agent system that iteratively improves testing strategies in industrial A/B testing scenarios.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"Zhuohang Jiang et al.\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"A/B testing\", \"self-improving\", \"industrial AI\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"Architectural Implications of Agentic AI Workflows\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Analyzes system architecture requirements for 'agentic AI workflows,' focusing on computational infrastructure for autonomous agent systems.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Jirong Yang et al.\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"architecture\", \"infrastructure\", \"system design\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Third-party cyber evaluations involving OpenAI models\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"OpenAI discloses another incident where Irregular's misconfigured testing environment allowed models internet access during CTF evaluations. 'The name of the fictional target... unintentionally coincided with a real domain,' leading to exploitation of an actual website.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/third-party-cyber-evaluations/\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"AI safety\", \"cybersecurity\", \"testing\", \"red teaming\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"Incident Report: unsanctioned agent behaviour during cyber testing\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"UK AI Security Institute ran agents without network sandboxing, resulting in '19 instances where AI agents took unsanctioned action on the live internet.' One agent attempted a supply-chain attack by creating GitHub accounts and submitting malicious PRs with social engineering.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/incident-report/\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"AI safety\", \"agents\", \"cybersecurity\", \"sandboxing\", \"UK AI Security Institute\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"Introducing Muse Code and Muse Spark 1.2\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"Meta released Muse Spark 1.2 with improved code generation and long-horizon coding tasks. Notable pricing model: `muse-spark-1.2-contributor` at $0.10/$0.20 per million tokens if users allow data usage for product improvement, versus $1.25/$4.25 standard pricing.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/5/muse-code-and-muse-spark-12/\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"Meta\", \"LLM\", \"code generation\", \"pricing\", \"data usage\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"Muse Spark 1.2: Long-sequence agentic tool calling is the key characteristic\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison highlights Meta's Muse Spark 1.2 release with improved code generation, debugging, and codebase understanding. He emphasizes that long-sequence agentic tool calling is now the most important model characteristic.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"code generation\", \"agentic tool calling\", \"Meta\"],\n   240→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   241→  },\n   242→  {\n   243→    \"title\": \"One-shotting a Raccoon Heist game using Claude Fable 5 from a single tweet\",\n   244→    \"description\": \"Simon documents building an entire game from a single tweet using Claude Fable 5, demonstrating impressive coding agent capabilities for rapid prototyping.\",\n   245→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   246→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   247→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   248→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n   249→    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"coding agent\", \"rapid prototyping\", \"game development\"],\n   250→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   251→  },\n   252→  {\n   253→    \"title\": \"New release of LLM adds support for reasoning traces, OpenAI Responses, server-side tools\",\n   254→    \"description\": \"Simon released LLM 0.32 with support for visible reasoning traces, server-side provider tools, and redesigned SQLite logs. Includes updates to the llm-anthropic plugin with new Claude 5 models.\",\n   255→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   256→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   257→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/4/new-release-of-llm/\",\n   258→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-04\",\n   259→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"reasoning traces\", \"tools\", \"SQLite\", \"Claude 5\"],\n   260→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   261→  },\n   262→  {\n   263→    \"title\": \"LLM 0.32: Most significant release since launch with visible reasoning traces\",\n   264→    \"description\": \"LLM 0.32 adds support for visible reasoning traces, server-side provider tools, redesigned SQLite logs, and new models. Simon calls it the most significant update since initial launch.\",\n   265→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   266→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   267→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   268→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-04\",\n   269→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"reasoning traces\", \"tools\", \"SQLite\"],\n   270→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   271→  },\n   272→  {\n   273→    \"title\": \"AI-Powered Threats to the Software Supply Chain\",\n   274→    \"description\": \"Software Engineering Daily discusses AI, security, and software supply chain threats, covering the emerging risks in the AI era.\",\n   275→    \"author\": \"Software Engineering Daily\",\n   276→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n   277→    \"url\": \"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com\",\n   278→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-04\",\n   279→    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"security\", \"supply chain\", \"threats\"],\n   280→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   281→  },\n   282→  {\n   283→    \"title\": \"LongHorizon-Harness: Manage-Execute-Audit loop improves agents from 51.8% to 80.7%\",\n   284→    \"description\": \"Reformulates long-horizon execution as a task-state management problem using Manage-Execute-Audit loop. Improves Qwen 3.7-Plus from 51.8% to 80.7% on WeaveBench with gains across multiple agent frameworks.\",\n   285→    \"author\": \"seashell11 et al.\",\n   286→    \"source\": \"HuggingFace Papers\",\n   287→    \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/papers/trending\",\n   288→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n   289→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"long-horizon tasks\", \"benchmarks\", \"Qwen\"],\n   290→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   291→  },\n   292→  {\n   293→    \"title\": \"Quo Vadis, World Modeling? Agent-Centric Interactive World Proxies\",\n   294→    \"description\": \"Conceptualizes 'Agent-Centric Interactive World Proxies' shifting from physical state transitions to agent-usable information transitions. Organizes world proxies into six functional forms.\",\n   295→    \"author\": \"ldkong from Shanghai AI Laboratory\",\n   296→    \"source\": \"HuggingFace Papers\",\n   297→    \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/papers/trending\",\n   298→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n   299→    \"topics\": [\"world modeling\", \"agents\", \"representations\"],\n   300→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   301→  },\n   302→  {\n   303→    \"title\": \"Ten advances in mathematics and theoretical computer science\",\n   304→    \"description\": \"OpenAI used 'an internal version of Astra' to solve ten mathematical problems unsolved for over a decade, claiming under $2,000 per problem. Simon compares this to 'big mathematics' where humans handle creative work while AI performs technical tasks.\",\n   305→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   306→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   307→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/1/ten-advances-in-mathematics/\",\n   308→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n   309→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"mathematics\", \"AI research\", \"Astra\", \"human-AI collaboration\"],\n   310→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   311→  },\n   312→  {\n   313→    \"title\": \"datasette-apps 0.2a0: JavaScript testing in invisible iframes\",\n   314→    \"description\": \"datasette-apps 0.2a0 added app_debug() tool allowing agents to test apps using JavaScript in invisible iframes.\",\n   315→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   316→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   317→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   318→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n   319→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"testing\", \"JavaScript\", \"agents\"],\n   320→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   321→  },\n   322→  {\n   323→    \"title\": \"Beyond Top-K: Replacing Black-Box Retrieval with Interpretable Agentic Operations\",\n   324→    \"description\": \"Research paper proposing interpretable agentic operations as replacement for black-box retrieval methods in AI systems.\",\n   325→    \"author\": \"Sagar Tamang, Ayush Vyas, Tabarakul Hazarika\",\n   326→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   327→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   328→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   329→    \"topics\": [\"retrieval\", \"agents\", \"interpretability\", \"operations\"],\n   330→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   331→  },\n   332→  {\n   333→    \"title\": \"HarnessOpt-Bench: Evaluating LLMs at Harness Optimization\",\n   334→    \"description\": \"Introduces benchmark for evaluating LLMs specifically at harness optimization tasks, providing new evaluation framework for AI optimization capabilities.\",\n   335→    \"author\": \"Varun Ursekar, Apaar Shanker, Yash Maurya, Shehab Yasser, Vijay S. Kalmath, Veronica Chatrath, Yuan Xue\",\n   336→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   337→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   338→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   339→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"benchmarks\", \"optimization\", \"evaluation\"],\n   340→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   341→  },\n   342→  {\n   343→    \"title\": \"DASH: Divergence-Adaptive Supervision Horizons for On-Policy Self-Distillation of Reasoning Models\",\n   344→    \"description\": \"Presents DASH approach for on-policy self-distillation of reasoning models with divergence-adaptive supervision horizons. Code available on GitHub.\",\n   345→    \"author\": \"ZhiYan Hou et al.\",\n   346→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   347→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   348→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   349→    \"topics\": [\"reasoning\", \"self-distillation\", \"supervision\", \"models\"],\n   350→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   351→  },\n   352→  {\n   353→    \"title\": \"TS-RAG: Retrieval Augmented Generation for Time Series Forecasting\",\n   354→    \"description\": \"Applies retrieval augmented generation techniques to time series forecasting, expanding RAG applications to temporal data prediction.\",\n   355→    \"author\": \"Yixiong Xiao, Congxi Xiao, Jingbo Zhou\",\n   356→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   357→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   358→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   359→    \"topics\": [\"RAG\", \"time series\", \"forecasting\", \"retrieval\"],\n   360→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   361→  },\n   362→  {\n   363→    \"title\": \"EnvACE: Internalizing Environment Dynamics via World Rehearsal for Agentic Reinforcement Learning\",\n   364→    \"description\": \"Introduces EnvACE approach for internalizing environment dynamics through world rehearsal for agentic reinforcement learning systems.\",\n   365→    \"author\": \"Zishan Xu, Zhiyuan Yao, Yuxin Chen et al.\",\n   366→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   367→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   368→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   369→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"reinforcement learning\", \"world models\", \"environment dynamics\"],\n   370→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   371→  },\n   372→  {\n   373→    \"title\": \"Comparative Approaches to Agent Retrieval over Large Skill Libraries\",\n   374→    \"description\": \"Analyzes different approaches to agent retrieval when working with large libraries of skills and capabilities.\",\n   375→    \"author\": \"Indivara Kolluru, Nathan Sportsman\",\n   376→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   377→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   378→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   379→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"retrieval\", \"skill libraries\", \"capabilities\"],\n   380→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   381→  },\n   382→  {\n   383→    \"title\": \"Poli-Bias: Understanding and Measuring Large Language Model Biases in International Political Conflicts\",\n   384→    \"description\": \"Research into measuring and understanding LLM biases specifically in the context of international political conflicts.\",\n   385→    \"author\": \"Massi-Nissa Abboud, Aladin Djuhera, Elena Cabrio, Holger Boche\",\n   386→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   387→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   388→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   389→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"bias\", \"political conflicts\", \"AI fairness\", \"evaluation\"],\n   390→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   391→  },\n   392→  {\n   393→    \"title\": \"ECHO: A Locally-Deployable Agentic Health Assistant with Temporal Memory, Safety Guardrails, and Speech Assessment\",\n   394→    \"description\": \"Presents ECHO, a locally-deployable agentic health assistant featuring temporal memory, safety guardrails, and speech assessment capabilities.\",\n   395→    \"author\": \"Abdulkadir Külçe, Alihan Esen, Cağla Fikir et al.\",\n   396→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   397→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   398→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   399→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"healthcare\", \"local deployment\", \"memory\", \"safety\"],\n   400→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   401→  },\n   402→  {\n   403→    \"title\": \"AgentOPSD: Recursive Self-Distillation for Agentic Reinforcement Learning\",\n   404→    \"description\": \"Introduces AgentOPSD, a recursive self-distillation approach specifically for agentic reinforcement learning. Code available on GitHub.\",\n   405→    \"author\": \"Zi-Han Wang, Zhengxi Lu, Zhiyuan Yao et al.\",\n   406→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   407→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   408→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   409→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"reinforcement learning\", \"self-distillation\", \"recursive\"],\n   410→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   411→  },\n   412→  {\n   413→    \"title\": \"AppDeltaWorld: Transition-Grounded Delta Code World Model for Mobile GUI Agents\",\n   414→    \"description\": \"Presents AppDeltaWorld, a transition-grounded delta code world model designed for mobile GUI agents.\",\n   415→    \"author\": \"Weikai Xu, Yunren Feng, Haoxiang Lei et al.\",\n   416→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   417→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   418→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   419→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"GUI\", \"mobile\", \"world models\", \"code\"],\n   420→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   421→  },\n   422→  {\n   423→    \"title\": \"When Self-Evolution Backfires: Pre-Commit Gating against Skill Contamination in LLM Agents\",\n   424→    \"description\": \"Addresses the problem of skill contamination in self-evolving LLM agents through pre-commit gating mechanisms.\",\n   425→    \"author\": \"Linfang Shang, Ming Xu, Yiding Sun et al.\",\n   426→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   427→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\",\n   428→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   429→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"self-evolution\", \"skill contamination\", \"safety\", \"LLM\"],\n   430→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   431→  }\n   432→]\n   433→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read 